// "Underlord" — Dungeon Keeper: imps dig marked rock (gold veins pay out) and claim the floor; claimed tiles give mana,
// new imps cost mana and each one costs more. Gold is kept in the heart and treasuries (their size caps it). Painted
// rooms attract creatures through a claimed portal (lair for all, a library for warlocks, a workshop for trolls, a big
// hatchery for bile demons, training for dark mistresses, a graveyard for vampires); creatures eat at the hatchery,
// sleep in the lair, want wages on payday and leave when unhappy, and level up by training and fighting. The library
// researches the keeper spells (sight of evil, lightning, heal) and dark arts. The hand picks up, drops and slaps;
// one creature can be possessed. Heroes from the surface invade now and then. Lose the heart and you lose.
// Not yet here (engine plan): traps and doors, prison / torture / temple, the computer keeper sending creatures to dig.
